@startuml CloudWarehouse_Deployment_Diagram
title Deployment Diagram — Environment Topology

skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #F0F8FF
  BorderColor #2980b9
}

node "Developer Workstation\n(local dev / demo)" as Local {
  artifact "Browser\nindex.html" as A1
  artifact "dotnet.exe\nCloudWarehouse.Backend.dll" as A2
  database "SQL Server\nDB: CloudWarehouse" as A3
}

node "GitHub Actions\n(CI pipeline)" as CI {
  artifact "dotnet SDK 9" as B1
  artifact "coverage-report\n(uploaded artifact)" as B2
  component "Workflow: ci.yml" as WF
}

node "Future production\n(planned)" as Future #E0E0E0 {
  artifact "App Service / IIS" as F1 #D0D0D0
  artifact "Azure SQL / managed SQL" as F2 #D0D0D0
}

A1 -[#2980b9,thickness=2]-> A2 : HTTP :5001\nREST + static files
A2 -[#27ae60,thickness=2]-> A3 : Connection string\nDefaultConnection

WF -[#34495e,dashed]-> B1 : uses
WF -[#34495e,dashed]-> B2 : publishes

note right of A2
  **Depends on:** SQL Server running
  **Start:** dotnet run --project CloudWarehouse.Backend
end note

note bottom of CI
  Trigger: push / PR to main
  Steps: restore -> test -> coverage report
end note

Future ..[hidden].. Local : future migration

@enduml

' 1. Primary deployment is local: browser, API process, and database on one workstation.
' 2. CI is a separate environment on GitHub Actions; output is test results and coverage HTML.
' 3. We document a planned cloud deployment but did not implement it for the course MVP.
